Chimera is a derivative fork of BizHawk (https://github.com/TASEmulators/BizHawk).

The upstream BizHawk repository combines an MIT-licensed C# frontend by the
BizHawk team with many emulation cores under a variety of licenses, and its
license file therefore describes the whole as a heterogeneous combination. In
this fork, all emulation cores and their support machinery have been removed:
what remains is the BizHawk team's original MIT-licensed work - the frontend
and its supporting libraries - plus Chimera's own modifications and new work,
which are provided under the same MIT License. Copyright in the code inherited
from BizHawk belongs to the BizHawk team; copyright in Chimera's modifications
and in all new work authored for Chimera belongs to Sergio Martin.

Exceptions, clearly separable from the MIT-licensed sources:

- extern/ contains third-party native libraries built from source during the
  build (SDL2, Lua, zstd, SQLite, OpenAL Soft, cimgui, luasocket, and
  supporting projects), vendored as pinned git submodules, each under its own
  open-source license (see each submodule's license file); they are compiled
  to separate dynamic libraries loaded at runtime.
- Emulation cores are NOT part of this repository. They are loaded at runtime
  as external, self-contained packages, each carrying its own license (a core
  package derived from a GPL emulator is a GPL work, for example). Consult
  each package's own license.
- tests/suite is a vendored regression suite whose provenance and
  licensing (including TASVideos movies under CC-BY 2.0) are described in
  tests/suite/README.md.

The terms themselves are in LICENSE: the MIT License, for all of the BizHawk
team's original work and for Chimera's modifications and new work.
